 hand-rolling (or adopt one of these libraries).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan item 1: 'A real alternative exclusive leg on Windows — msvcrt.locking(fd, LK_NBLCK, n) (or LockFileEx via ctypes)'","Web (docs.python.org msvcrt; runebook.dev; en.wpmm.jp) confirms portalocker/filelock are the canonical libraries handling msvcrt.locking on Windows and fcntl on POSIX automatically","search_files 'portalocker' -> (no matches); search_files 'filelock' -> (no matches): plan reinvents the seam with no dependency present","Plan gives no comparison to or rejection rationale for these established libraries"],"finding":"The plan hand-rolls a cross-platform exclusive-lock seam (msvcrt.locking / LockFileEx alongside fcntl.flock) without considering the established prior-art libraries portalocker and filelock, which exist specifically to abstract the fcntl-vs-msvcrt split. Repo search confirms neither library is currently a dependency, so this is a genuine in-house reinvention of a well-trodden abstraction. The plan's demanding staleness-proof invariant (fcntl_held=True reclamation) is plausibly a valid reason to hand-roll — those libraries do not offer that proof — but the plan never names the prior art or justifies deviating from it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f557087e1ede61798","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'What a correct fix requires', item 1 ('A real alternative exclusive leg on Windows — msvcrt.locking(fd, LK_NBLCK, n) (or LockFileEx via ctypes)')","norm_id":"n5bb6946d7b7747e2","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/maintainer asks why rebar hand-rolls Windows locking instead of using a maintained cross-platform lib","Future maintenance burden of ctypes/msvcrt edge cases that portalocker already handles"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In 'What a correct fix requires', add a sentence noting that portalocker/filelock are the standard fcntl-vs-msvcrt abstractions, and justify hand-rolling on the grounds that neither exposes the kernel-mediated, dies-with-process reclamation proof (fcntl_held=True) this lock depends on — or adopt one and layer the staleness proof on top.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Commit to ONE Windows exclusive primitive and state how it locks the empty .ticket-write.lock (e.g. write/seek to a fixed sentinel byte before msvcrt.locking(fd, LK_NBLCK, 1), or the exact LockFileEx OVERLAPPED offset/length), so the region-lock semantics on a 0-byte file are specified rather than assumed.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8175,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'msvcrt.locking(fd, LK_NBLCK, n) (or LockFileEx via ctypes) — with the same kernel-mediated, dies-with-the-process exclusivity'","lock.py:204/249 open the lock file with os.O_CREAT | os.O_RDWR — the file is empty (0 bytes) when locked","msvcrt.locking documented behavior: locks nbytes of the file starting at the current file pointer; region semantics on a zero-length file differ from flock's whole-inode advisory lock","resolve_symbol: msvcrt.locking / ctypes.windll UNRESOLVED on this POSIX host (expected; not evidence of absence) — surface is UNVERIFIED here"],"finding":"The plan offers msvcrt.locking(fd, LK_NBLCK, n) and LockFileEx-via-ctypes as interchangeable alternatives ('or') without committing to one or reconciling their different region-locking semantics against an EMPTY lock file. msvcrt.locking locks a byte range relative to the current file position and conventionally requires the region to exist in the file; .ticket-write.lock is opened O_CREAT and is 0 bytes, so locking n>=1 bytes of an empty file is an unaddressed feasibility question.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f11e23b7cf35969f1","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"\"What a correct fix requires\" item 1 (msvcrt.locking(fd, LK_NBLCK, n) (or LockFileEx via ctypes))","norm_id":"n7ea4c8bb16356632","priority":0.0825,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A Windows writer opens the empty .ticket-write.lock and msvcrt.locking(fd, LK_NBLCK, 1) fails or no-ops because there is no byte at offset 0 to lock, silently defeating exclusivity","The two candidate primitives take different offset/length arguments, so 'or' hides a real design choice that changes the staleness proof"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_clai